{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And YHWH hurled</b> — He cast, by way of metaphor. And the meaning is that He cast him from the dry land; therefore they could not return to the dry land, for this was only at the place where the sea joins with the river, and it is near the dry land, for it is always treacherous for ships. And the proof that it was so is that he said: <i>you cast me into the deep, into the heart of the seas, and the river surrounded me</i>." "<b>The ship reckoned</b> — like <i>when a land sins against me</i>."], :book :jonah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Jonah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=19&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:58.788657738Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}